FRITZ!Box failover helper for OPNsense.

Watches a FRITZ!Box Cable WAN line via UPnP or TR-064 (WANIPConnection:1
GetStatusInfo) and pings to several internet addresses forced through
the cable gateway, while the gateway itself is monitored against the
FRITZ!Box to avoid false dpinger alarms.
On sustained failure it swaps the gateway monitor IP to a dead
address so dpinger reports 100% loss and OPNsense's native gateway
groups fail over, without disabling the gateway. When the cable line
is healthy again the normal monitor IP is restored.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.9

* Public IP services configurable (default ifconfig.me and ip.me),
  asked in order via IPv4; at least two required
* At least two internet test addresses required

1.8

* Pushover messages include the current public IPv4 address

1.7

* Keep measuring the cable line during a test failover (no decisions)

1.6

* Optional Cloudflare DNS switch of a CNAME (e.g. WireGuard host name)
* Optional Pushover notifications on failover and failback
* Both are retried until they succeed (the line is down at that moment)
* "Check Cloudflare" and "Send test push" buttons

1.5

* Switch history (kept across reboots): last switch to backup, backup
  active since (with live duration) and a table of the last switches

1.4

* Plugin version shown on the page, linking to the project on GitHub

1.3

* Fix: checks stopped after a failover because dpinger inherited the
  internal lock (now lockf(1), which never passes the lock on)
* Countdown with progress bar during a test failover

1.2

* Test failover button: real failover for 2 minutes, same path as an outage
* Gateway selection from a dropdown of the found gateways
* Better readable loss statistics
* Install command uses curl instead of fetch

1.1

* Restarting the service ("Apply", reboot, update) keeps an active failover
* Uninstalling stops the service and restores the normal monitor IP
* FRITZ!Box status via UPnP without login; TR-064 login is optional
* TR-064 is paused for 15 minutes after a failed login
* No switching during the first 2 minutes after boot
* Configuration is locked while the monitor IP is changed
* Switching no longer adds entries to the configuration history
* "Restore normal monitor IP" button, fixed "Test connection" on 26.1
* IP fields no longer accept wildcards
* Less logging during an outage

